      "mergedPostDetails": "Base Post by peq42:\nhttps://unity.com/releases/2022-1#platform-optimizations\nUnity 2022 just recently came out, and among other things, it brought late latching and motion vectors. Both of those things bring great performance improvements for VR users, as can be seen here: \nhttps://developer.oculus.com/blog/optimizing-vr-graphics-with-late-latching/\nand \nhttps://developer.qualcomm.com/blog/improving-vr-performance-using-motion-estimation-opengl-extensions#:~:text=In%20VR%2C%20motion%20vectors%20are,render%20at%20a%20lower%20framerate.\nSo I suggest that the next engine update be to unity 2022. It'll benefit VR users quite a bit.",
